1
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:14,597
You pulled it off again.
I knew you'd do a good job.

2
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:19,686
You look like you didn't sleep well.

3
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:24,941
Well, it's understandable.

4
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:29,821
6,018,000 won.

5
00:00:31,114 --> 00:00:32,449
Thank you for your hard work.

6
00:00:32,949 --> 00:00:34,242
I'm done.

7
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:35,660
What?

8
00:00:36,536 --> 00:00:38,955
But the next job pays 200 times more.

9
00:00:41,416 --> 00:00:44,419
People died right in front of me.
What kind of…

10
00:00:44,502 --> 00:00:49,674
If it'd really happened,
it'd be all over the news right now.

11
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:54,220
So that wasn't real?

12
00:00:58,016 --> 00:00:58,933
Mr. Hyeok-jun.

13
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:03,855
In my eyes,
you have a knack for this work.

14
00:01:04,355 --> 00:01:06,608
Do you think I'm some kind of psycho?

15
00:01:07,859 --> 00:01:08,818
Damn it.

16
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:11,654
How would you even have a knack
for this crazy work?

17
00:01:14,032 --> 00:01:15,200
Someone

18
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:18,703
must do this work.

19
00:01:20,997 --> 00:01:24,918
What's the most important thing to you
right now?

20
00:01:27,378 --> 00:01:29,047
Think it over carefully.

21
00:01:31,424 --> 00:01:33,593
The answer will be near you.

22
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:40,892
I'll see you again.

23
00:01:55,490 --> 00:01:57,534
REST YOUR WEARY BODY
WE WILL REMEMBER YOU

24
00:01:58,118 --> 00:02:01,830
MAY DELIVERY WORKER KIM CHANG-GYU
REST IN PEACE

25
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:22,392
Why?

26
00:02:23,268 --> 00:02:24,644
Does it hit close to home?

27
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:30,984
Are you following me?

28
00:02:31,067 --> 00:02:31,901
What?

29
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:34,904
Hey, I was standing here first.
You came after.

30
00:02:38,283 --> 00:02:39,492
Shopping?

31
00:02:39,576 --> 00:02:41,286
I'm sorry. I must've thought…

32
00:02:41,369 --> 00:02:43,037
Aren't you curious?

33
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:45,957
About what Spider Staffing Agency does?

34
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:48,293
Sorry?

35
00:02:49,836 --> 00:02:52,380
Whether all of it is real or an illusion.

36
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:55,717
Shall we have that cup of tea now?

37
00:03:01,764 --> 00:03:05,894
You've probably never heard
of a labor accident investigator.

38
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:09,063
WORKERS' COMPENSATION UNION
EUM YEON-JOO, ACCIDENT INVESTIGATOR

39
00:03:09,147 --> 00:03:11,232
A labor accident investigator?

40
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:14,110
There are many agencies in our country.

41
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:19,115
You could say that strange cases
that don't warrant police involvement

42
00:03:19,199 --> 00:03:22,035
but aren't really suited for civil court

43
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:24,871
usually come to us.

44
00:03:25,872 --> 00:03:28,208
What kind of strange cases?

45
00:03:29,918 --> 00:03:30,835
For example…

46
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:37,508
a staffing agency lures people in
with high-paying part-time jobs,

47
00:03:38,259 --> 00:03:40,970
but strangely,
everyone who does these jobs

48
00:03:41,763 --> 00:03:43,890
either develops some kind of problem

49
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:46,559
or goes missing.

50
00:03:48,603 --> 00:03:49,729
Anything to say?

51
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:56,194
I can help you only if you tell me now.

52
00:04:16,005 --> 00:04:17,215
MAJOR FIRE BREAKS OUT AT HOSPITAL OFFSITE

53
00:04:17,340 --> 00:04:18,466
"A fire…"

54
00:04:19,550 --> 00:04:21,219
CAUSE UNKNOWN
CASUALTIES UNQUANTIFIABLE

55
00:04:21,344 --> 00:04:24,347
That's not what I saw.

56
00:04:24,430 --> 00:04:25,723
It wasn't an accident.

57
00:04:26,557 --> 00:04:29,519
I tried to believe it was a hallucination,
but then it was…

58
00:04:29,602 --> 00:04:31,688
Do you really think it's that easy

59
00:04:33,022 --> 00:04:34,357
to make someone hallucinate?

60
00:04:34,983 --> 00:04:36,609
That vividly?

61
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:40,613
Thank you.

62
00:04:41,114 --> 00:04:42,365
For having the courage.

63
00:04:44,784 --> 00:04:46,327
I'll see you again, right?

64
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:53,459
I quit that part-time job.

65
00:05:52,810 --> 00:05:56,481
DEAD-END JOB

66
00:05:57,690 --> 00:06:00,610
EPISODE 3
MILKMAN VLOG

67
00:06:02,779 --> 00:06:06,115
Did you make some money?
Enough to buy me clothes and shoes?

68
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:09,577
They say you'll die
if you do something out of character.

69
00:06:11,412 --> 00:06:12,705
Do you like it that much?

70
00:06:12,789 --> 00:06:15,708
Well, my feet hurt a little.

71
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:20,129
You'd better do well on the interview.

72
00:06:21,422 --> 00:06:22,465
I'm off.

73
00:06:23,341 --> 00:06:24,675
Hey, wait.

74
00:06:25,343 --> 00:06:26,427
What now?

75
00:06:33,810 --> 00:06:34,644
For me?

76
00:06:48,574 --> 00:06:49,909
I got it on Karrot Market.

77
00:06:50,410 --> 00:06:52,203
It's not fake, they said.

78
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:54,205
So why?

79
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:58,918
I thought if you had a luxury item on you…

80
00:07:01,212 --> 00:07:03,381
you might value yourself more.

81
00:07:07,176 --> 00:07:08,678
I saw that your pull-up bar fell.

82
00:07:09,679 --> 00:07:11,389
And there was rope in the trash.

83
00:07:14,725 --> 00:07:16,477
Just saying, don't do anything stupid.

84
00:07:18,187 --> 00:07:19,647
- Ji-yoon, that was--
- Bye.

85
00:07:31,534 --> 00:07:34,495
You worked on that over there?

86
00:07:41,127 --> 00:07:45,089
VERY GOOD EMPLOYMENT AGENCY

87
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:48,009
Logistics Group 1, get on the bus!

88
00:07:49,927 --> 00:07:51,137
Logistics Group 1!

89
00:07:52,513 --> 00:07:54,891
Move quickly! We haven't got all day!

90
00:07:54,974 --> 00:07:56,309
Time, people!

91
00:07:56,809 --> 00:07:59,896
Don't stack them up and push them forward!
Sort these quickly!

92
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:02,815
Scan the barcodes quickly!

93
00:08:02,899 --> 00:08:04,734
Hurry up!

94
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:12,366
Seriously, it's killing me.

95
00:08:14,118 --> 00:08:17,663
<i>At Hanbit Logistics, we follow</i>
<i>a 2-hour work, 20-minute break schedule</i>

96
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:21,125
<i>as per the guidelines</i>
<i>of the Ministry of Employment and Labor.</i>

97
00:08:21,626 --> 00:08:23,961
Could I have a sip too?

98
00:08:25,296 --> 00:08:26,172
Sorry?

99
00:08:26,255 --> 00:08:29,383
You said it was okay to share the cup
since we're both blood type AB.

100
00:08:29,467 --> 00:08:30,468
Byeon Hyeok-jun.

101
00:08:30,551 --> 00:08:31,552
Kwak Byeong-cheol?

102
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:34,680
- Yeah.
<i>- Hanbit Logistics is with you.</i>

103
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:37,475
What are you doing here?
Wasn't your family well-off?

104
00:08:37,975 --> 00:08:40,603
I used to eat at your place all the time.

105
00:08:42,271 --> 00:08:44,982
I know, right? We used to be well-off.

106
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:48,528
Hey, I was watching you from a distance.

107
00:08:49,278 --> 00:08:50,863
You were working damn hard.

108
00:08:51,364 --> 00:08:53,074
Damn, I should.

109
00:08:53,574 --> 00:08:56,244
But it's tough. I'll spend more
on pain meds than I earn.

110
00:08:56,744 --> 00:08:59,830
It's because you're new.
You get used to it if you hang in there.

111
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:06,254
But if you've got no other job,
you gotta do it, right?

112
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:12,426
HEAD OF SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

113
00:09:13,302 --> 00:09:15,930
<i>Are you still mulling it over?</i>

114
00:09:16,722 --> 00:09:19,141
<i>Will you miss out on a gig</i>
<i>that pays 200 times more?</i>

115
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:21,686
Two hundred…

116
00:09:24,855 --> 00:09:25,690
What's that?

117
00:09:27,316 --> 00:09:28,526
What?

118
00:09:29,026 --> 00:09:30,069
A debt collector?

119
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,488
Hey!

120
00:09:32,572 --> 00:09:34,115
Get to work, Kwak Byeong-cheol!

121
00:09:34,198 --> 00:09:35,533
Okay, I'm coming!

122
00:09:37,034 --> 00:09:38,786
That bastard always picks on me.

123
00:09:38,869 --> 00:09:39,704
See ya.

124
00:09:40,454 --> 00:09:41,289
Bye.

125
00:09:42,164 --> 00:09:45,751
Hey, but still, don't overwork yourself.

126
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:49,422
You might clock out for real.
Last week, someone had a heart attack--

127
00:09:49,505 --> 00:09:52,008
- Goddammit! Hurry up!
- I'm off.

128
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:55,469
- You're working overtime today.
- That's terrible.

129
00:09:55,553 --> 00:09:57,471
<i>Always working with the workers…</i>

130
00:10:09,942 --> 00:10:11,736
STILL MULLING IT OVER?
WILL YOU MISS A 200X-PAYING GIG?

131
00:10:11,861 --> 00:10:12,903
Forget about it.

132
00:10:13,404 --> 00:10:14,363
Forget it.

133
00:10:18,242 --> 00:10:19,452
DELETE ALL

134
00:10:34,216 --> 00:10:36,469
<i>Hello, this is the Xenon HR team.</i>

135
00:10:36,552 --> 00:10:40,264
<i>Is this Mr. Byeon Hyeok-jun?</i>
<i>You've passed the initial screening.</i>

136
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:42,016
<i>I have? Really?</i>

137
00:10:42,099 --> 00:10:46,729
<i>Can you come for an interview</i>
<i>today at 4 p.m.? I'll send the address.</i>

138
00:10:57,948 --> 00:10:59,700
INTERVIEWEES THIS WAY

139
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:11,629
- Ms. Kim Si-yeon.
- Yes?

140
00:11:11,712 --> 00:11:12,713
Yes, Ms. Kim.

141
00:11:13,214 --> 00:11:15,007
- Here you go.
- Hello.

142
00:11:17,301 --> 00:11:18,511
Mr. Moon Jae-eun.

143
00:11:18,594 --> 00:11:19,512
Yes, I'm here.

144
00:11:19,595 --> 00:11:21,514
"High Seed Big Tech Briefing"?

145
00:11:24,934 --> 00:11:26,936
- You'll be great and make lots of money.
- Yes.

146
00:11:28,145 --> 00:11:30,356
Damn it. I fucking knew it.

147
00:11:34,610 --> 00:11:36,195
Mr. Byeon Hyeok-jun!

148
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:42,535
Mr. Byeon Hyeok-jun,
your interview is up next.

149
00:11:46,330 --> 00:11:48,040
Is Mr. Byeon Hyeok-jun here?

150
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:52,795
Yes, Mr. Byeon.

151
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:54,588
Here, wear this first and--

152
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:57,842
RÉSUMÉ
BYEON HYEOK-JUN

153
00:12:01,011 --> 00:12:03,431
Then I guess you'll just be poor.

154
00:12:06,434 --> 00:12:08,018
Han, Han Do-yeon?

155
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:10,354
Ms. Han Do-yeon.

156
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:12,940
Han…

157
00:12:16,152 --> 00:12:16,986
What?

158
00:12:17,987 --> 00:12:19,029
Look.

159
00:12:20,656 --> 00:12:23,325
I skipped eating and bailed on my mom
just to show up today.

160
00:12:24,535 --> 00:12:27,079
I even transferred two buses to get here.
But this…

161
00:12:28,789 --> 00:12:30,666
- This is a pyramid scheme.
- A pyramid…

162
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:33,836
- This is a high seed, big tech--
- That's what a pyramid scheme is!

163
00:12:36,505 --> 00:12:37,590
A pyramid scheme?

164
00:12:38,716 --> 00:12:40,509
No, it's not.

165
00:12:41,135 --> 00:12:44,054
He doesn't know what he's talking about.

166
00:12:53,355 --> 00:12:54,440
Hello?

167
00:12:54,523 --> 00:12:56,442
<i>Hey, Hyeok-jun.</i>

168
00:12:56,942 --> 00:12:58,402
When do you get off work?

169
00:12:58,903 --> 00:13:00,571
Let's get some frozen pork belly.

170
00:13:00,654 --> 00:13:02,656
<i>Frozen pork belly sounds nice.</i>

171
00:13:03,157 --> 00:13:04,742
<i>But now's not really…</i>

172
00:13:14,001 --> 00:13:16,086
What the hell is this, man?

173
00:13:16,587 --> 00:13:19,048
They said it was rhabdomyolysis.

174
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:20,716
Or something like that.

175
00:13:22,218 --> 00:13:24,386
I almost clocked out for good, man.

176
00:13:26,931 --> 00:13:29,517
- When do you get discharged?
- I don't know.

177
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:35,940
If I don't get better in a few days,
I might need kidney dialysis.

178
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:50,704
[HANBIT LOGISTICS] RE: WORK INJURY CLAIM

179
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:53,207
"The company bears
no responsibility whatsoever"?

180
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:56,919
Those fucking bastards, seriously.

181
00:13:58,754 --> 00:14:00,965
The company won't pay
for the hospital bills?

182
00:14:02,383 --> 00:14:05,386
I don't even have private insurance.
Maybe I should just die.

183
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:17,022
Yes, Mr. Hyeok-jun.

184
00:14:18,315 --> 00:14:21,193
So have you found another job?

185
00:14:21,694 --> 00:14:22,611
For minimum wage?

186
00:14:22,695 --> 00:14:25,781
<i>Sir, I need some money urgently.</i>

187
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:27,199
<i>That job that pays 200 times…</i>

188
00:14:33,581 --> 00:14:36,000
HEUKRAN OFFICETEL, MILKMAN
200 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE, 10 P.M. - 6 A.M.

189
00:14:39,044 --> 00:14:40,045
Milk

190
00:14:41,046 --> 00:14:42,047
delivery?

191
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:43,716
<i>Yes, milk delivery.</i>

192
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:49,638
The wage is based on an eight-hour day,
but the job actually takes about an hour.

193
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:53,017
You won't find a sweeter gig than this.

194
00:14:54,101 --> 00:14:58,188
<i>That should be more than enough</i>
<i>to cover your friend's hospital bills.</i>

195
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:30,512
Okay.

196
00:15:59,583 --> 00:16:02,002
<i>You won't find a sweeter gig than this.</i>

197
00:16:02,086 --> 00:16:02,962
A sweet gig.

198
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:11,887
YEONGSAN MILK

199
00:16:16,892 --> 00:16:18,060
Eleven bottles.

200
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:20,187
Don't be scared, all right?

201
00:16:20,938 --> 00:16:24,692
HEUKRAN OFFICEL, MILKMAN
200 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE, 10 P.M. - 6 A.M.

202
00:16:28,237 --> 00:16:30,406
- Here for a delivery?
- You scared me.

203
00:16:32,491 --> 00:16:33,784
Yes.

204
00:16:38,288 --> 00:16:39,540
Delivering them all?

205
00:16:41,291 --> 00:16:43,377
Yes, of course.

206
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:45,546
Finish within an hour.

207
00:16:45,629 --> 00:16:47,965
Or you might not be able
to leave this place.

208
00:16:49,049 --> 00:16:51,844
Wait, I won't be able to leave?

209
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:53,971
Keep it to one hour.

210
00:16:56,849 --> 00:16:58,475
Okay.

211
00:17:00,394 --> 00:17:01,353
Hold on.

212
00:17:05,482 --> 00:17:06,775
What's that in your bag?

213
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:08,193
What?

214
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:13,323
This here is…

215
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:14,992
Well, actually…

216
00:17:17,494 --> 00:17:18,829
What is all of this?

217
00:17:20,581 --> 00:17:22,458
Are you here to rob the place?

218
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:25,210
No.

219
00:17:26,503 --> 00:17:27,880
Pick them up when you leave.

220
00:17:27,963 --> 00:17:29,089
Okay.

221
00:17:36,972 --> 00:17:38,724
You have one hour. One hour.

222
00:17:44,146 --> 00:17:46,356
You'll be fine.
Just avoid any delivery mistakes.

223
00:17:46,940 --> 00:17:48,358
Although it won't be easy.

224
00:18:02,289 --> 00:18:04,458
This is…

225
00:18:05,334 --> 00:18:08,003
In case something goes wrong…

226
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:09,713
Damn, what the hell am I saying?

227
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:17,513
This is Hyeok-jun's Milkman Vlog.

228
00:18:19,556 --> 00:18:23,185
Six bottles to the second floor,
four to the fourth, one to the fifth.

229
00:18:23,268 --> 00:18:25,312
Beginning delivery.

230
00:18:43,831 --> 00:18:45,124
As fast as I can.

231
00:18:45,207 --> 00:18:47,751
232, 223.

232
00:18:49,169 --> 00:18:50,796
215.

233
00:18:51,588 --> 00:18:52,673
Unit 210.

234
00:18:53,257 --> 00:18:54,091
206.

235
00:18:54,925 --> 00:18:57,219
206, and next is 202.

236
00:19:01,181 --> 00:19:02,891
Unit 202.

237
00:19:04,434 --> 00:19:05,519
204.

238
00:19:06,019 --> 00:19:07,104
203.

239
00:19:08,063 --> 00:19:09,314
201.

240
00:19:10,649 --> 00:19:11,984
Why isn't it here?

241
00:19:16,321 --> 00:19:18,615
232, 233.

242
00:19:26,582 --> 00:19:27,875
What the heck?

243
00:19:30,377 --> 00:19:31,420
Shit.

244
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:34,131
I'll move on since there's no time.

245
00:19:41,889 --> 00:19:43,223
Who's there?

246
00:19:52,900 --> 00:19:54,484
What's the matter with this?

247
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:56,445
Damn it.

248
00:19:59,531 --> 00:20:01,241
Let's move on for now.

249
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:14,713
Oh God.

250
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:34,608
Let's get the fourth floor over with.
It's just one unit.

251
00:20:38,946 --> 00:20:39,821
Oh shit.

252
00:20:43,158 --> 00:20:45,160
What the hell? Why are they all 444?

253
00:20:57,756 --> 00:20:59,591
Damn it, what a bad omen.

254
00:21:06,223 --> 00:21:07,599
Four-four… What?

255
00:21:09,643 --> 00:21:11,311
Four-four…

256
00:21:15,315 --> 00:21:18,360
Four divided by four plus…

257
00:21:23,532 --> 00:21:25,534
Are they messing with me or something?

258
00:21:27,828 --> 00:21:28,912
444.

259
00:21:36,837 --> 00:21:37,671
Let's go.

260
00:21:44,219 --> 00:21:45,304
What the…

261
00:21:46,638 --> 00:21:48,098
Why?

